Online:Imperial Districts:
{{Mod Header|Imperial City}}{{Trail|Places/Alliance War}}[[File:ON-map-Imperial City.jpg|thumb|left|A map of the Imperial City]][[File:ON-mapicon-ImperialDistrict.png|right]]
The '''Imperial Districts''' are the battle-torn residential and commercial areas of the [[Online:Imperial City|Imperial City]]. Each district is a combined close-quarters PvE and PvP area, with gameplay similar to that in the rest of [[Online:Cyrodiil|Cyrodiil]]. However, [[Online:Siege Weapons|Siege Weapons]] cannot be used in the districts. Each district has one PvP capture point located on the bridge leading to the inaccessible gates of the Palace District. There are also a limited number of PvE [[Online:Imperial City#Quests|quests]] available; each district functions as a [[Online:Quest Hubs|quest hub]] containing one story quest, and each also has one repeatable daily quest.

Every district has a small [[Online:Alliances|Alliance]] [[Online:Alliance War#Safe Zones|rally point]] which is accessed from the Alliance Base in the [[Online:Imperial Sewers|Imperial Sewers]], as well as an access point for all alliances into one of the sewer sections. Districts also contain [[Online:Trophy Vaults|Trophy Vaults]] which can be opened by collecting a certain number of [[Online:Trophies|Trophies]] from creatures within the city, and three of the districts contain special gear [[Online:Crafting Sites|Crafting Sites]]. Each district contains two [[Online:Patrolling Horrors|Patrolling Horror]]s, powerful bosses that drop a large number of [[Online:Tel Var Stones|Tel Var Stones]]. Only one Patrolling Horror is active at a time, however. [[Online:Imperial City Portals|Portals]] to Coldharbour are also scattered throughout the districts.

To claim a district, the attackers need to hold the capture point on the Palace District bridge for a short period of time, after defeating the attendant NPC alliance soldiers. Once a district is claimed, NPCs of the controlling faction will appear there to help guard the flag. Note that faction soldiers do not appear anywhere else within the district. Being in control of a district grants the controlling alliance the ability to respawn at that district's rally point instead of at the Alliance Base in the Sewers. It also grants a 33% increase to the number of [[Online:Tel Var Stones|Tel Var Stones]] earned by players of that alliance while in any of the Imperial City districts (but not the Sewers). This bonus is cumulative, and stacks to 198% if one alliance controls all six districts.
