[[File:ON-icon-weapon-Trueflame.png|Trueflame|right]]
During [[Online:Events/2014#Early Access|early access]], it was possible to very rarely obtain {{Item Link|Trueflame|itemid=54267|level=60|quality=2}} while fishing in [[Online:Stonefalls|Stonefalls]]. This was a [[Online:Veteran|Veteran Rank]] sword that was part of the [[Online:Arms of Infernace|Arms of Infernace]] item set. It was quickly removed before the game's official release with [[Online:Patch/1.0.1|Patch 1.0.1]], but existing copies of the sword can still be found in-game and can be traded to other players.

As part of ESO's tenth anniversary celebrations, a [[Online:Trueflame Sword Replica Style|Trueflame Sword Replica]] was made available as a weapon style. During the [[Online:Anniversary_Jubilee#Anniversary_Jubilee_2024|Anniversary Jubilee 2024]] event, all fishing nodes had a rare chance to drop a {{Item Link|Bound Style Page: Trueflame Sword Replica|itemid=204475|quality=5}} in reference to the original bug from 2014.
{{NewLine}}

==Fishing Buffs==
===Champion Point Perks===
There are two Champion perks associated with fishing. Both are in the [[Online:Craft|Craft]] tree, and both are active (i.e. must be slotted to take effect). These are [[Online:Reel Technique|Reel Technique]] and [[Online:Angler's Instincts|Angler's Instincts]]. The former reduces the time needed for a fish to bite by 25%; the latter increases the chance to snag a rare fish and stacks with other bonuses such as the one from Lure Allure detailed below. 

===Fish Eye===
[[File:ON-activity-Fish Eye.jpg|thumb|right|Fish Eye]]
:''Increases Magicka and Stamina Recovery by x and grants keen eyes toward fish.''
'''Fish Eye''' is a status effect gained by drinking '''[[Online:Hissmir Fish-Eye Rye|{{ESO Quality Color|5|Hissmir Fish-Eye Rye}}]]'''. In addition to a level-scaled buff to {{ESO Magicka Link||Recovery}} and {{ESO Stamina Link||Recovery}}, the drink grants "keen eyes" similar to the [[Online:Nodes#Skill Perks|Keen Eye]] perks available for crafting material [[ON:Nodes|nodes]]. With this status effect, fishing holes will appear to glow, and the water type will be displayed when you approach (e.g. "River Fish", "Spawning Fish", etc). While the glow effect may be useful in highlighting fishing holes, the secondary effect is largely obsolete since water types are now automatically displayed even without this drink active.

===Lure Allure===
:''Increases Max Health and Max Magicka. Additionally, fish may be drawn to you.''
'''Lure Allure''' is a buff gained by eating '''[[Online:Artaeum Pickled Fish Bowl|{{ESO Quality Color|4|Artaeum Pickled Fish Bowl}}]]'''. In addition to a level-scaled increase to your maximum {{ESO Health Link}} and {{ESO Magicka Link}}, the food increases your chance of fishing rare fish.
{{NewLine}}

==={{Anchor|Sharp's Patience}}{{ESO NE}}===
[[File:ON-icon-keepsake-Sharp's Handmade Fishing Lure.png|right|Sharp's Handmade Fishing Lure]]
:''Fish bite at an increased rate and have a higher chance of being trophy fish.''
[[Online:Sharp's Patience|Sharp's Patience]] is the [[Online:Companions|Companion]] Perk granted by [[Online:Sharp-as-Night|Sharp-as-Night]], a Companion added by the [[Online:Necrom (Chapter)|Necrom]] Chapter. When he is with you, his perk causes fish to bite at an increased rate, and also increases your chances of catching a trophy fish. Trophy fish obtained due to this perk will have the Companion icon displayed next to them on the UI when caught. Note that the perk does not reduce your chance to hook special items, nor does it affect the rate at which you catch non-trophy fish that can be fileted for Perfect Roe; it only reduces your chance to catch bait.

Summoning Sharp at max rapport after he reaches level 20 will grant you {{Item Link|collectid=11452|Sharp's Handmade Fishing Lure}}, a Keepsake which permanently unlocks the Sharp's Patience perk without the need to have him as your active Companion.

==Fishing Achievements==
[[File:ON-render-Fishing on High Isle.jpg|thumb|right|Fishermen on High Isle]]
There are many [[ON:Fishing Achievements|achievements associated with fishing]]. Every zone except the starter islands has 12 rare fish you can catch. Catching all of the rare fish in a zone will give you that zone's achievement. If you get all of the major zone achievements in one alliance, you'll receive another achievement for that alliance. Get all three of those, along with the starter island achievements and the separate ones for Cyrodiil and Coldharbour, and you'll receive the rare Master Fisher achievement. Note that the fish on the starter islands are not necessary for the alliance fishing achievements, but they are necessary for the Master Fisher achievement. Completing the Master Fisher achievement grants the title "Master Angler".

Craglorn Angler and the DLC achievements are not needed to earn the Master Fisher achievement. Fish Boon Angler is a quest-related [[ON:Holiday Events Achievements|holiday event achievement]].

