Online:Recipes/deprecated:
{{Trail|Items}}{{Deprecated|Update 6}} [[File:ON-icon-quest-Scroll 01.png|right]]
There are 351 '''recipes''' to be collected in total: 171 {{ESO Quality Color|f|'''Standard'''}} recipes, 135 {{ESO Quality Color|s|'''Difficult'''}} recipes, and 45 {{ESO Quality Color|e|'''Complex'''}} recipes. Learning a recipe will remove it from your inventory, but in exchange, you will learn how to craft its meal indefinitely. Recipes can be found in Trunks, Wardrobes, Desks, Nightstands, and the likes. The recipe received when you loot a container is based on your ''character level'', and not the zone you are in. To cook food or brew a beverage, you must have the required [[Online:Provisioning|provisioning]] skills. If you do, simply visit a cooking fire found in most towns to begin combining [[Online:Provisioning Ingredients/deprecated|ingredients]]. Eating food and drinking beverages temporarily gives your [[Online:Attributes|attributes]] a bonus when consumed. However, food and beverage bonuses do not stack, so you have to pick only one.

*There are two skills required to craft food and beverages.
**[[Online:Provisioning|Recipe Improvement]] ranges from 1 to 6 and lets you make higher Level-Requirement meals.
**[[Online:Provisioning|Recipe Quality]] ranges from 1 to 3 and allows you to craft {{ESO Quality Color|f|'''Standard'''}}, {{ESO Quality Color|s|'''Difficult'''}}, and {{ESO Quality Color|e|'''Complex'''}} versions of recipes.
***Recipes have a {{ESO Quality Color|s|'''Difficult'''}} version if they require you to be Level 10 or above to consume its food or beverage.
***Recipes have a {{ESO Quality Color|e|'''Complex'''}} version if they require you to be Level 35 or above to consume its food or beverage.


*Recipe ingredients are broken down as follows.

:{{ESO Quality Color|f|Primary ingredient and ''Secondary ingredient''}}
:{{ESO Quality Color|s|+Difficult-Quality ingredient}}
:{{ESO Quality Color|e|+Complex-Quality ingredient 1 and Complex-Quality ingredient 2}}
*The {{ESO Quality Color|f|''secondary ingredient''}} of a recipe is determined by its Recipe Improvement requirement (''RI'').
*Higher Recipe Quality (RQ) recipes use ingredients in an additive way. This means that to craft a {{ESO Quality Color|e|'''Complex'''}} food or beverage, you must also use the required ingredients of its {{ESO Quality Color|f|'''Standard'''}} and {{ESO Quality Color|s|'''Difficult'''}} counterparts.
*{{ESO Quality Color|e|Complex-Quality}} ingredients are always used in pairs. For example, {{ESO Quality Color|e|{{icon|f|Garlic|24}} Garlic and {{icon|f|Yeast|24}} Pepper}} always go together, and you will never find a purple recipe that requires {{ESO Quality Color|e|{{icon|f|Yeast|24}} Pepper}} and another {{ESO Quality Color|e|Complex-Quality}} ingredient.

All {{ESO Quality Color|e|'''Complex'''}} recipes have "Consummate" in the recipe title, but the prefix of {{ESO Quality Color|s|'''Difficult'''}} recipes depends on the recipe's category.
